我从来没有比和她共度一生更确定的事情了。

00:49:38.000 --> 00:49:50.000
I'm completely in love with her and even though she doesn't understand my obsession with how I met your mother, rolling her eyes every time Ted starts talking about the one, she knows the impact the show has had in shaping me.
我完全爱上了她，尽管她不理解我对如何遇见你母亲的痴迷，每次特德开始谈论这个人时她都会翻白眼，但她知道这部剧对塑造我的影响。

00:49:50.000 --> 00:49:59.480
So had I not majored in engineering and instead gone to some design school four years earlier, I probably would not have met her and would still be cursing my time after high school.
因此，如果我没有主修工程，而是四年前去了一些设计学校，我可能就不会遇到她，并且仍然会咒骂我高中毕业后的时间。

00:49:59.480 --> 00:50:11.780
This realization made such an impact on me that for my senior dissertation, I wrote a paper on how I met your mother and the causal significance of seemingly unimportant moments and decisions in our lives, the butterfly effect.
这种认识对我产生了很大的影响，以至于在我的毕业论文中，我写了一篇关于我如何遇见你母亲的论文，以及我们生活中看似不重要的时刻和决定的因果意义，即蝴蝶效应。

00:50:11.780 --> 00:50:13.940
It was my way of saying, thank you.
这是我说谢谢的方式。

00:50:13.940 --> 00:50:18.820
An ode to the series for making me understand that you can't jump straight to the end.
对这个系列的颂歌让我明白你不能直接跳到最后。

00:50:18.820 --> 00:50:21.260
The journey is the best part.
旅程是最好的部分。

00:50:21.260 --> 00:50:25.380
Today, like Ted, I get to do what I've always wanted to do as a kid.
今天，像泰德一样，我可以做我小时候一直想做的事情。

00:50:25.380 --> 00:50:28.179
I sketch and design cars for a living.
我以素描和设计汽车为生。

00:50:28.179 --> 00:50:37.070
And like Ted, who got to design the Spokane National Bank Tower at a young age, the first car I've designed is all set to launch next year.
就像年轻时就设计了斯波坎国家银行大厦的泰德一样，我设计的第一辆汽车也将于明年推出。

00:50:37.070 --> 00:50:50.150
I hope I get to live the dream with my girlfriend by my side, and it's all because of that one decision that was forced on me by my folks after high school, so I could be at the right place, at the right time.
我希望我能和女朋友一起实现梦想，这都是因为高中毕业后我的父母强迫我做出的一个决定，这样我就能在正确的时间出现在正确的地方。

00:50:50.150 --> 00:50:52.590
I cannot thank you guys enough for making how I met your mother.
我非常感谢你们让我认识了你们的母亲。

00:50:52.590 --> 00:50:54.349
It's not just a show to me.
对我来说这不仅仅是一场表演。

00:50:54.349 --> 00:50:56.949
It's a guidebook to living life.
这是一本生活指南。

00:50:56.949 --> 00:50:57.980
That's awesome.
太棒了。

00:50:57.980 --> 00:50:58.980
Man.
男人。

00:50:58.980 --> 00:50:59.980
Great letter.
很棒的信。

00:50:59.980 --> 00:51:00.980
Congrats on that car.
恭喜那辆车。

00:51:00.980 --> 00:51:01.980
Can it be called the Mosby?
可以叫莫斯比吗？

00:51:01.980 --> 00:51:02.980
Just asking.
只是问问。

00:51:02.980 --> 00:51:03.980
It hasn't gone to press yet.
它还没有付印。

00:51:03.980 --> 00:51:04.980
Can we still get it in there?
我们还能把它放进去吗？

00:51:04.980 --> 00:51:05.980
That's so wonderful.
那真是太好了。

00:51:05.980 --> 00:51:07.980
Thank you for that letter.
谢谢你的那封信。

00:51:07.980 --> 00:51:20.980
And again, we're just so thrilled that this show we made has been such an important part of people's lives.
再说一遍，我们非常高兴我们制作的这部剧成为人们生活中如此重要的一部分。

00:51:20.980 --> 00:51:21.980
So thank you.
所以谢谢你。

00:51:21.980 --> 00:51:22.980
Keep those letters coming.
让这些信继续来。

00:51:22.980 --> 00:51:23.980
Keep those voice notes coming.
让这些语音笔记不断出现。

00:51:23.980 --> 00:51:25.980
And we will see you next time.
我们下次再见。

